Summary of modifications made in flockr (see `git log` for the exact changes):

1. Rename. The product, crate, binary, config and state directories
   (`~/.config/flockr`, `flockr-dev` for debug builds), socket and log file names,
   CLI output and UI text, `TERM_PROGRAM`, `FLOCKR_*` environment variables,
   `flockr:<id>` agent report sources, integration hook script names and markers,
   plugin manifest (`flockr-plugin.toml`, `min_flockr_version`), remote bridge
   markers, and config values (`ui.toast.delivery = "flockr"`,
   `[ui.toast.flockr]`, `--right-click flockr`) were renamed from herdr.
2. Compatibility layer (`src/legacy_herdr.rs`). Panes also export the legacy
   `HERDR_*` variables; env vars read by the server and CLI fall back from
   `FLOCKR_*` to `HERDR_*` (except instance identity variables); `herdr:<id>`
   report sources are accepted as aliases of `flockr:<id>`; the old `"herdr"`
   config and CLI values are accepted as deprecated aliases. `~/.config/herdr`
   is never read or migrated.
3. Hosting. Self-update, release notes, product announcements, remote installer
   downloads and agent-detection manifest fetches point at
   https://github.com/Rambarani/flockr (constants in `src/product.rs`) instead of
   herdr.dev and the upstream GitHub repository.
4. Feature: sidebar agents are grouped under workspace headers.
5. Feature: configurable notification sounds with built-in tones and a settings
   picker.
6. Feature: upstream herdr watcher. flockr checks the upstream herdr releases
   in the background (`[upstream]` config, `src/upstream/`), notifies inside the
   app, and `flockr upstream sync|apply` merges a release into flockr through an
   isolated git worktree. The upstream version flockr is synced to is recorded
   in `.flockr/upstream-base`.
7. Feature: UI additions: renaming workspaces and agents (double-click, right-click
   menu, keys), a which-key popup, a command palette, an agent preview popup, an
   agent dashboard, and collapsible workspace groups in the agent sidebar.
8. Feature: jobs (`src/jobs/`). Scheduled commands (`job.toml`, every or cron)
   with timeouts, login-shell environment capture, catch-up runs, a Jobs overlay
   and the `flockr job` CLI, including system jobs (ids starting with `system.`).
9. Feature: feeds. Jobs can publish a feed of items (feed format v1, `flockr feed`
   CLI, `flockr feed adapt workbox`), shown in a sidebar section and a Feed overlay
   with categories, a detail pane, item actions and sync now.
10. Feature: handoff and decisions. A job can ask whether to start an agent tab
    after a run (`[handoff]`, `flockr decision` CLI, Decisions tab).
11. Feature: job authoring kit. `flockr job new|validate|build|schema|skill`,
    `flockr job run --dry-run`, JSON Schemas under `docs/next/api/`, and the
    `flockr-jobs` skill (`skills/flockr-jobs/`).

Artwork. herdr's logo, social card and screenshot are not used. assets/logo.svg and
assets/logo.png are flockr's own mark. The notification sounds in assets/sounds
come from herdr under the same Apache-2.0 license.

